intro=a.add('sections',2,'A school office may know that a visitor is a student. That does not make the visitor a teacher or permit access to a teacher guide. Authentication establishes an identity or session; authorization applies the service’s permission rules to an action and a resource. In a real system, roles come from trusted server-side records or verified claims under the system’s policy, not a label the visitor writes on a request. Our example starts with trusted classroom fixtures rather than implementing a login system.')
